.TH AMATL 1 "August 2026" "amatl 0.1.0-rc.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amatl \- generalist multi-source search
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amatl
[\fB--config-file\fR \fIPATH\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AMATL searches multiple governed sources through one Rust core. Search remains
lightweight; Deep enrichment, persistence, Trafilatura and Chromium are optional.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B search
Run the lightweight multi-provider search pipeline.
.TP
.B deep
Run Search followed by bounded document enrichment and evidence extraction.
.TP
.B ingest
Extract evidence from one explicit local file.
.TP
.B providers, config, cache, doctor
Inspect effective configuration and local capabilities.
.TP
.B serve
Start the loopback UI, REST API and MCP surface.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I amatl.toml
Optional configuration file. Secrets must be supplied through environment variables.
.SH SECURITY
The default server binds to loopback and requires a bearer token. A non-loopback
bind requires authentication and TLS. See SECURITY.md and the project documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://github.com/IA-Alex/amatl
